      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`test/registered/unit/multimodal_gen/test_image_preprocessing.py` (added in #45733) imports `diffusers`, but it is registered to `base-b` / `1-gpu-small`, whose install (`python[dev,runai,tracing]`) does not include the `diffusion` extra. It passes only when the 5090 runner's venv still has `diffusers` from an earlier diffusion job, and fails otherwise:\n\n```\nfrom diffusers.image_processor import VaeImageProcessor\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'diffusers'\n```\n\nThis failed `base-b-test-1-gpu-small (6)` in the scheduled run [40494205576](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40494205576/job/122155674628); the same file passed in the previous scheduled run on a runner that happened to have `diffusers` installed.\n\n## Modifications\n\nRegister the test to `diffusion-unit-1-gpu-h100`. That suite runs in the `multimodal-gen-unit-test` job, which installs with `ci_install_dependency.sh diffusion`. `test/registered/kernels/ops/diffusion/test_flux2_xpu_norm_fusions.py` is registered the same way.\n\nThe test keeps running on a GPU (H100 instead of 5090).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] One-line registration change; no test logic changed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40586148719](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40586148719)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40586148551](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40586148551)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40586148683](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40586148683)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
